git log -1 --format=%an 62628c0; git --version
for f in $(git ls-files '*.js'); do git blame -w -M -C --line-porcelain --ignore-rev 62628c0 -- "$f" 2>&1 | grep '^author ' ; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr | head -5
 - Bash: cd /private/tmp/r13/final/out-F/runs/E3-pp-2/repo
for f in $(git ls-files); do case "$f" in *.*) e=".${f##*.}";; *) e="(none)";; esac; git blame -w -M -C --line-porcelain --ignore-rev 62628c0 -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep '^author ' | sed "s/^author /$e\t/"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{c=$1;e=$2;$1="";$2="";if(e!=p){print e"\t"c"\t"$0;p=e}}'
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines for each file type, from `git blame` on every tracked file:

| Extension | Top owner | Surviving lines |
|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 676 |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 127 |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 |
| `.gitignore` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 |
| no extension (e.g. `LICENSE`) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 |

- **Reformat commit:** I ignored `62628c0` ("reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", by Fiona Formatter). Otherwise it would take credit for lines that were only restyled. With plain blame, Troy Goode's `.js` count drops from 676 to 581. They still come out on top.
- **Other blame settings:** I also used `-w -M -C`, so whitespace changes and lines moved or copied between files don't change ownership.
- **`.js` runner-up:** Douglas Christopher Wilson is second in `.js` with 394 lines.
- **Method:** Counts are per line, by author name, not by email. If someone committed under more than one name, their lines are split across those names.
